    "result_text": "All 34 tests pass. The change is complete and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string membership tier with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133):\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` (string) response property with `membershipLevel`, an `int32` in the range 1\u20133, marked `readOnly`. This drives the generated `OwnerDto`, so the response now exposes `membershipLevel` and no longer exposes `membershipTier`.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Replaced `getMembershipTier()` with `getMembershipLevel()`, computing: start at 1, +1 when an email is present, +1 when `namesakeCount` is 0, capped at 3. (The old GOLD-by-household-size logic is gone; household size no longer influences the level \u2014 level 4 is reserved for tenure.)\n\n**`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 The create audit line now records `membershipLevel={}` alongside the id it already logged, so the audit trail records the level instead of the tier.\n\nThe MapStruct mapper needed no change \u2014 it maps by property name, which now resolves `membershipLevel` on both sides.\n\nAll existing and new acceptance tests (including Cp15, Cp21, Cp23, Cp24) pass: **34 run, 0 failures**.",
